Standard fonts
--------------

The fourteen standard-font metric modules are numbers derived from the
Adobe AFM files PDFKit 0.20.2 generates from. The raw .afm files are not
installed by the rock. They remain in vendor/pdfkit/lib/font/data/ with
Adobe's notice. The generated modules say:

    Copyright (c) 1985, 1987, 1989, 1990, 1997 Adobe Systems Incorporated.
    All Rights Reserved.

    Helvetica, Times, Courier, Symbol, and ZapfDingbats are trademarks of
    their owners. The Helvetica AFM notice names Linotype-Hell AG.

    This file and the 14 PostScript(R) AFM files it accompanies may be
    used, copied, and distributed for any purpose and without charge,
    with or without modification, provided that all copyright notices are
    retained; that the AFM files are not distributed without this file;
    that all modifications to this file or any of the AFM files are
    prominently noted in the modified file(s); and that this paragraph is
    not modified. Adobe Systems has no responsibility or obligation to
    support the use of the AFM files.

A Lua metric module is a modification of that generated file: the same
numbers, written as a Lua table. The notice above is the one those
modules carry.

ICC profile
-----------

PDF/A output embeds the sRGB profile PDFKit 0.20.2 ships at
lib/mixins/data/sRGB_IEC61966_2_1.icc. The profile's own copyright
string is:

    Copyright International Color Consortium, 2015

The description string in the profile is "sRGB2014" / "IEC 61966-2-1
Default RGB Colour Space - sRGB". The bytes are loaded from a Lua module
so the rock install does not depend on a file beside the source. This is
not the older HP/Microsoft sRGB notice. That notice is not in the profile
this tag ships.

Test fonts and images
---------------------

Fonts and images under test/assets/ are for the comparator. They are not
installed by the rock. Each one is named in test/assets/NOTICE.

GoodDog.ttf is not included. Its name table says "Copyright (c) 1996 by
Ethan Dunham - Fonthead Design. All rights reserved." and carries no
redistribution grant. The embedded-font programs use Droid Sans Mono
instead, which has the same property those programs were written for:
no GSUB, GPOS, kern, or morx table.

The PDFKit 0.20.2 tag also carries GoodDog, Apple's Chalkboard, and
Apple's Palatino Bold under docs/fonts and examples/fonts. Those copies
are gitignored. They stay on disk after a local clone of the tag, and
they are not part of this repository.
